      "created_at": "2022-08-17T04:24:28Z",
      "updated_at": "2022-08-17T04:25:30Z",
      "body": "To give some more information about it.\r\n\r\nIt's not about loading the google font, but the fact to send the user IP to google (which will store it) to load the font, making nocodb sharing private data which is against privacy law in many countries (including all the countries in Europe due to GDPR).\r\n\r\nhttps://complianz.io/google-fonts-and-gdpr-does-it-work/\r\n\r\nhttps://blog.runcloud.io/google-fonts-gdpr/\r\n\r\nhttps://thehackernews.com/2022/01/german-court-rules-websites-embedding.html\r\n\r\nSo yes it would be good practice to store the fonts as an asset to avoid having to ask consent / add the annoying popup.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
